-- title:
--   Finite étale level rings of j on the X₀(p) model
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime (with $p \neq 0$ as a natural number) and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \neq p$. Write $F = \mathbb{Q}(\,\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q},d}(j) : d \mid p,\ d \neq 0\,)$ for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the $q$-expansions of $j$ at the divisors of $p$, let $j_{\mathrm{full}} \in F$ be the class of $j$ itself, and let $A$ be the finite-$j$ chart subalgebra $\mathrm{chartAlg}\,\mathbb{Z}\,F\,\{j_{\mathrm{full}}\}$ of $F$, with $u \in A$ the element $j_{\mathrm{full}}$. The assertion is the existence of a nonzero $\mathrm{avoid} \in (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)[X]$ and a nonzero $c_0 \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ such that for every monic $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ with $\deg g \geq 1$ whose reduction $g \bmod \ell$ is irreducible in $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)[X]$ and coprime to $\mathrm{avoid}$, and with $g \nmid c_0$, there is an integer $c \neq 0$ not divisible by $\ell$ with the following property: for every nonzero $f \in \mathbb{Z}$ divisible by $c$, the level ring $B = A[1/f]/(g(u))$ — the quotient of the localisation of $A$ away from the image of $f$ by the ideal generated by $g$ evaluated at the image of $u$ — is, as an algebra over $\mathbb{Z}[1/f] = \mathrm{Localization.Away}\,f$, module-finite, étale, free as a module, of $\mathbb{Z}[1/f]$-rank $(p+1)\deg g$, and of rank at the stalk $(p+1)\deg g$ at every prime of $\mathbb{Z}[1/f]$. Note that irreducibility of $g \bmod \ell$ is required, not merely separability.
--
--   This produces finite étale multisections of constant degree $(p+1)\deg g$, cut out by level sets of the coordinate $j$ (of degree $p+1$ on $X_0(p)$), on the finite-$j$ chart of the integral model of $X_0(p)$ over $\mathbb{Z}[1/f]$. It supplies the local splitting data used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_locallySplitPools_of_le_span_of_ne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_locallySplitPools_of_le_span_of_ne) in the treatment of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of that model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_HpoolLevelRing_exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin.lean

